WEBVTT

1
00:55:30.338 --> 00:55:41.338
Hallelujah! Is everyone a little happy today? Yes? Wonderful. Oh, nice.

2
00:55:41.338 --> 00:55:50.138
A step deeper. That is how I have named my collection talk today, as it is called.

3
00:55:50.138 --> 00:55:55.938
Maybe it is nice to also take a step deeper. Of course, we all fasted together this week

4
00:55:55.938 --> 00:56:03.738
and also try to go a step deeper, seeking God. As we draw closer to God, He draws closer to us.

5
00:56:03.738 --> 00:56:08.938
And I also had a verse that we have seen a few times this week.

6
00:56:08.938 --> 00:56:13.938
And it actually applies to the returning of what we do and the sowing that we do.

7
00:56:13.938 --> 00:56:22.138
It would be very nice, so Romans 12, verses 1 and 2. And I will read it from the NBV.

8
00:56:22.138 --> 00:56:25.138
And it says brothers and sisters.

9
00:56:25.138 --> 00:56:35.138
I urge you, in view of God's mercy, to offer your bodies as a living, holy and pleasing sacrifice to God.

10
00:56:35.138 --> 00:56:39.138
For this is your true and proper worship.

11
00:56:39.138 --> 00:56:46.138
Do not conform to the pattern of this world, but be transformed by the renewing of your mind.

12
00:56:46.138 --> 00:56:53.138
Then you will be able to test and approve what God's will is—his good, pleasing and perfect will.

13
00:56:55.138 --> 00:57:01.138
We have seen this text several times this week, but if you look, it says pleasing twice.

14
00:57:01.138 --> 00:57:07.138
And pleasing means that if something is pleasing to someone, it makes them happy.

15
00:57:07.138 --> 00:57:11.138
Basically, it simply concerns making God happy.

16
00:57:12.138 --> 00:57:16.138
And that is something we do with every offering we bring.

17
00:57:16.138 --> 00:57:18.138
That we make God happy.

18
00:57:18.138 --> 00:57:22.138
I find it so beautiful that we can make God happy.

19
00:57:22.138 --> 00:57:24.138
That we can make God happy.

20
00:57:24.138 --> 00:57:28.138
There is only one through whom that can happen.

21
00:57:28.138 --> 00:57:30.138
That is Jesus.

22
00:57:30.138 --> 00:57:38.138
I want to highlight a few points from that, also for us to give, to bring us back.

23
00:57:38.138 --> 00:57:47.138
That we present ourselves as a living and holy, pleasing offering in His service.

24
00:57:47.138 --> 00:57:53.138
We can only be alive and holy and pleasing through Jesus.

25
00:57:53.138 --> 00:57:59.138
And it is true that we may take action.

26
00:57:59.138 --> 00:58:07.138
But we must do that in a measure of obedience, faith, and in His pure way.

27
00:58:08.138 --> 00:58:12.138
And bringing back sowing is a part of ourselves.

28
00:58:12.138 --> 00:58:19.138
What we may gather and invest time in is a part of ourselves.

29
00:58:19.138 --> 00:58:22.138
It is also an offering.

30
00:58:22.138 --> 00:58:28.138
And we may also present a part of ourselves in His service with that.

31
00:58:28.138 --> 00:58:30.138
And He wants all of us.

32
00:58:30.138 --> 00:58:35.138
He does not want just something we have put together ourselves.

33
00:58:36.138 --> 00:58:40.138
Or where we think, oh yes, that also needs to be done.

34
00:58:40.138 --> 00:58:43.138
That is not what He longs for.

35
00:58:43.138 --> 00:58:45.138
And how do we do that then?

36
00:58:45.138 --> 00:58:47.138
To bring a pleasing offering to God.

37
00:58:47.138 --> 00:58:52.138
That does not mean adapting ourselves to this hectic, fleeting world.

38
00:58:52.138 --> 00:58:57.138
Where we are just cursing at the microwave because it is not quick enough.

39
00:58:57.138 --> 00:59:01.138
We may adapt to His.

40
00:59:01.138 --> 00:59:03.138
To be His.

41
00:59:03.138 --> 00:59:07.138
And we may change our attitude, our mindset.

42
00:59:07.138 --> 00:59:10.138
To discover what God wants from you.

43
00:59:10.138 --> 00:59:14.138
What is good and perfect and pleasing to Him, as the text says.

44
00:59:14.138 --> 00:59:18.138
And if we do not conform to this world.

45
00:59:18.138 --> 00:59:23.138
And we take a little distance from what we have done during the week.

46
00:59:23.138 --> 00:59:26.138
Then we may actually also do for our return.

47
00:59:26.138 --> 00:59:29.138
For God is quite particular when it comes to offerings.

48
00:59:30.138 --> 00:59:33.138
If we look in the Bible, there are numerous examples of this.

49
00:59:33.138 --> 00:59:35.138
Cain and Abel.

50
00:59:35.138 --> 00:59:38.138
With Cain's offering, things do not go well at all.

51
00:59:38.138 --> 00:59:40.138
If we look at Abraham.

52
00:59:40.138 --> 00:59:44.138
God did not ask Abraham for Ishmael.

53
00:59:44.138 --> 00:59:46.138
He asked for Isaac.

54
00:59:46.138 --> 00:59:48.138
The pure.

55
00:59:48.138 --> 00:59:50.138
There are deeper lessons in this.

56
00:59:50.138 --> 00:59:57.138
And ultimately God provides for Abraham and Isaac does not need to be sacrificed at all.

57
00:59:57.138 --> 00:59:59.138
But his willingness was tested.

58
00:59:59.138 --> 01:00:02.138
And ultimately God provides.

59
01:00:02.138 --> 01:00:08.138
These are all deep lessons that relate to returning, to giving, to sowing.

60
01:00:08.138 --> 01:00:12.138
And this is what I want to bring today.

61
01:00:12.138 --> 01:00:18.138
I want to say something not only about the gift of today that we may bring back to the Father.

62
01:00:18.138 --> 01:00:20.138
But actually also cultivate an attitude within us.

63
01:00:20.138 --> 01:00:22.138
For we are all gathered here together.

64
01:00:22.138 --> 01:00:24.138
Jesus has brought us all together.

65
01:00:24.138 --> 01:00:26.138
And we are building.

66
01:00:26.138 --> 01:00:28.138
We are in the process of building.

67
01:00:28.138 --> 01:00:32.138
But when we build, we should not do it half-heartedly.

68
01:00:32.138 --> 01:00:35.138
But we should actually prefer to do it right the first time.

69
01:00:35.138 --> 01:00:41.138
We are perfect examples of how it often should not be done.

70
01:00:41.138 --> 01:00:44.138
And that is why we need Jesus.

71
01:00:44.138 --> 01:00:48.138
And that is why I want to ask to reflect on this.

72
01:00:48.138 --> 01:00:50.138
Also in the times to come.

73
01:00:50.138 --> 01:00:56.138
For I believe that when we are in a building process, it is not just a building process for that pile of stones that will come.

74
01:00:56.138 --> 01:00:59.138
It is a building process for you and for me.

75
01:00:59.138 --> 01:01:01.138
And that we may draw closer to God.

76
01:01:01.138 --> 01:01:07.138
And that we may be aware of what we can bring back to God to make Him happy.

77
01:01:07.138 --> 01:01:10.138
And that is why I want to ask this.

78
01:01:10.138 --> 01:01:17.138
That we bring our attitude seriously, our mindset seriously before God.

79
01:01:17.138 --> 01:01:19.138
And we do that actually very simply.

80
01:01:19.138 --> 01:01:23.138
Because Jesus died for us, we can just ask for it.

81
01:01:23.138 --> 01:01:26.138
Lord, what makes you happy?

82
01:01:26.138 --> 01:01:29.138
I really don't want to impose anything on anyone.

83
01:01:29.138 --> 01:01:31.138
I want it to come from within.

84
01:01:31.138 --> 01:01:34.138
I want us to grow together.

85
01:01:34.138 --> 01:01:35.138
In faith.

86
01:01:35.138 --> 01:01:38.138
For how beautiful it is to sow and see that God just provides again.

87
01:01:38.138 --> 01:01:40.138
And how God provides again.

88
01:01:40.138 --> 01:01:41.138
And how God provides again.

89
01:01:41.138 --> 01:01:43.138
And that He provides again.

90
01:01:43.138 --> 01:01:45.138
He keeps going.

91
01:01:46.138 --> 01:01:47.138
And that is good.

92
01:01:47.138 --> 01:01:49.138
Even if circumstances are sometimes unpleasant.

93
01:01:49.138 --> 01:01:51.138
He always provides.

94
01:01:52.138 --> 01:01:54.138
May we be thankful.

95
01:01:56.138 --> 01:01:58.138
And I think it is beautiful to stand up.

96
01:01:58.138 --> 01:02:02.138
And that we just give God the honor for this.

97
01:02:02.138 --> 01:02:05.138
Father, we give you the honor and the glory.

98
01:02:05.138 --> 01:02:09.138
For everything, Lord, is for your honor and for your glory.

99
01:02:09.138 --> 01:02:11.138
Lord that we worship you.

100
01:02:11.138 --> 01:02:14.138
Lord that we also pray and intercede.

101
01:02:14.138 --> 01:02:19.138
But also, Lord, that we may return what you have entrusted to us.

102
01:02:20.138 --> 01:02:22.138
Lord, I pray for a blessing over all of us.

103
01:02:22.138 --> 01:02:26.138
Lord, that we may grow in this process of building.

104
01:02:26.138 --> 01:02:29.138
If we build purely, then you can do something with that.

105
01:02:29.138 --> 01:02:33.138
And then you will show in your supernatural way that you are God.

106
01:02:33.138 --> 01:02:35.138
Lord, for this is how you want to work.

107
01:02:35.138 --> 01:02:42.138
Not in our human way, but in your own divine, royal way.

108
01:02:42.138 --> 01:02:48.138
Lord, that you may take us along, Lord, in growing as a royal priesthood.

109
01:02:48.138 --> 01:02:50.138
In the name of King Jesus. Amen.

110
01:02:50.138 --> 01:02:51.138
Amen.

