153
01:06:35.138 --> 01:06:50.138
If you have your Bible with you, please turn with me to the Chronicles.

154
01:06:50.138 --> 01:06:54.138
That is what we will be talking about in the coming time.

155
01:06:54.138 --> 01:07:01.138
We start at 1.

156
01:07:01.138 --> 01:07:09.138
Who read Psalm 78 yesterday or this morning?

157
01:07:09.138 --> 01:07:13.138
Yes? Thanks.

158
01:07:13.138 --> 01:07:20.138
You will find out what that has to do with the Bible study we will be doing in the next few weeks.

159
01:07:21.138 --> 01:07:27.138
For instead of preaching and shouting and doing backflips on a stage,

160
01:07:27.138 --> 01:07:31.138
we will be doing a Bible study in the coming time.

161
01:07:31.138 --> 01:07:36.138
Sometimes people ask me, can't we also have Bible studies in open church?

162
01:07:36.138 --> 01:07:43.138
To which my answer is, I hope that Sunday morning is jam-packed with God's Word.

163
01:07:43.138 --> 01:07:48.138
So that when the lingering congregation is together, we can do a Bible study together.

164
01:07:48.138 --> 01:07:54.138
Instead of presenting an anecdote on Sunday and organizing a Bible study somewhere on Wednesday

165
01:07:54.138 --> 01:07:57.138
and not everyone comes, then you miss a very large part of the church.

166
01:07:57.138 --> 01:08:00.138
I want to address God's Word on Sunday morning.

167
01:08:00.138 --> 01:08:02.138
As much as possible, so that we all receive this.

168
01:08:02.138 --> 01:08:06.138
So here is a real Bible study in the coming time.

169
01:08:10.138 --> 01:08:14.138
We started this year with 1 Chronicles chapter 28.

170
01:08:15.138 --> 01:08:20.138
And that is the statement of the theme for this year.

171
01:08:20.138 --> 01:08:22.138
Build My House.

172
01:08:22.138 --> 01:08:25.138
Last year it was Build The House.

173
01:08:25.138 --> 01:08:29.138
And this year Build My House is truly a commission.

174
01:08:29.138 --> 01:08:33.138
And I read that commission back in 1 Chronicles chapter 28.

175
01:08:33.138 --> 01:08:36.138
No, 1 Chronicles chapter 28, yes.

176
01:08:36.138 --> 01:08:43.138
And because we start there, it is important that we just take a step back

177
01:08:43.138 --> 01:08:49.138
and together do a study from which context this verse comes.

178
01:08:49.138 --> 01:09:01.138
As Christians, we should not be Christians who tie our faith to wall tiles with 1 verse

179
01:09:02.138 --> 01:09:07.138
and somewhere else a calendar with another verse

180
01:09:07.138 --> 01:09:13.138
and a Bible app that pings at a random time in the morning.

181
01:09:13.138 --> 01:09:15.138
and then you look at it and then another verse.

182
01:09:15.138 --> 01:09:20.138
And then to say that you are busy with God's Word.

183
01:09:20.138 --> 01:09:30.138
For if you do that, there is a danger that you do not study the actual Scripture yourself.

184
01:09:31.138 --> 01:09:36.138
For very often those wall tiles and those Bible apps

185
01:09:36.138 --> 01:09:45.138
are very often verses of encouragement and comfort and blessing and protection.

186
01:09:45.138 --> 01:09:49.138
It is all God's Word and they are all correct.

187
01:09:49.138 --> 01:09:51.138
And they are all 100% truth.

188
01:09:51.138 --> 01:09:56.138
But there is still so much more 100% truth.

189
01:09:57.138 --> 01:10:03.138
And we are going to, in the coming time, and that is why it is important that we always have the context of

190
01:10:03.138 --> 01:10:06.138
when we read a letter, we need to know what we are reading.

191
01:10:06.138 --> 01:10:09.138
What kind of letter is it that we are reading?

192
01:10:09.138 --> 01:10:14.138
And so now we have started with 1 Chronicles chapter 28

193
01:10:14.138 --> 01:10:16.138
and we need to know, yes but what is Chronicles?

194
01:10:16.138 --> 01:10:19.138
Why? What is this then?

195
01:10:20.138 --> 01:10:27.138
It is so important people, especially for us western people in the modern times we live in,

196
01:10:27.138 --> 01:10:30.138
that we know what we believe.

197
01:10:30.138 --> 01:10:34.138
That we truly know the depth of faith.

198
01:10:34.138 --> 01:10:42.138
For if we do not know the Old Testament, who is Jesus then?

199
01:10:43.138 --> 01:10:47.138
If we do not really read the Old Testament,

200
01:10:47.138 --> 01:10:51.138
and we are only busy, yes I do read the Old Testament,

201
01:10:51.138 --> 01:10:54.138
for recently I received a message from the Bible app, Jeremiah 29 verse 11,

202
01:10:54.138 --> 01:10:57.138
that God has good plans for my life, it lasts.

203
01:10:57.138 --> 01:11:00.138
Read the rest of that chapter once.

204
01:11:00.138 --> 01:11:02.138
Do you understand what I mean?

205
01:11:02.138 --> 01:11:10.138
But if we do not take the Old Testament as the true Word of God,

206
01:11:11.138 --> 01:11:17.138
and if we do not take the Old Testament so that it may shape us,

207
01:11:18.138 --> 01:11:20.138
who is Jesus then?

208
01:11:20.138 --> 01:11:26.138
For Jesus is the fulfillment of the Old Testament.

209
01:11:26.138 --> 01:11:30.138
The Old Testament hungered for Jesus.

210
01:11:30.138 --> 01:11:34.138
The Old Testament longed for Jesus.

211
01:11:35.138 --> 01:11:40.138
But if you do not read that, and if you are not engaged with it,

212
01:11:40.138 --> 01:11:44.138
who is Jesus once again?

213
01:11:44.138 --> 01:11:49.138
You run the risk of coming to church,

214
01:11:49.138 --> 01:11:55.138
and being caught up in the hype of the beautiful song.

215
01:11:55.138 --> 01:12:01.138
And today during the worship, and in the past ten days during the worship,

216
01:12:02.138 --> 01:12:07.138
I went up together with God and it was wonderful and amazing.

217
01:12:07.138 --> 01:12:10.138
Thank you, Lord, hallelujah.

218
01:12:10.138 --> 01:12:11.138
So nice.

219
01:12:11.138 --> 01:12:18.138
And those dopamine levels in your body, they go up.

220
01:12:18.138 --> 01:12:21.138
And you also hear, wow, this is cool, this is amazing.

221
01:12:21.138 --> 01:12:25.138
And we have such a great band, and they are doing so well.

222
01:12:26.138 --> 01:12:34.138
But if your faith is based on the wow factor of the open church,

223
01:12:34.138 --> 01:12:37.138
then you will run into serious problems.

224
01:12:37.138 --> 01:12:41.138
That is life-threatening.

225
01:12:41.138 --> 01:12:46.138
And that is why so many Christians today are leaving the faith.

226
01:12:46.138 --> 01:12:53.138
Because today's Christians often surf on the wow factor of the church.

227
01:12:53.138 --> 01:12:56.138
But the church is not always wow.

228
01:12:56.138 --> 01:13:02.138
And also, if we surf on the wow factor of the church,

229
01:13:02.138 --> 01:13:06.138
then the church has to perform every time.

230
01:13:06.138 --> 01:13:11.138
And then we have to do our best every time to make it even cooler.

231
01:13:11.138 --> 01:13:15.138
Wow, were you at that one Christmas service?

232
01:13:15.138 --> 01:13:16.138
Wow, that was awesome.

233
01:13:16.138 --> 01:13:18.138
Were you at that one Easter service?

234
01:13:18.138 --> 01:13:22.138
Because during the Easter service, wow, what they sang then.

235
01:13:22.138 --> 01:13:24.138
And the choir then.

236
01:13:24.138 --> 01:13:27.138
Wow, and they also did a play.

237
01:13:27.138 --> 01:13:29.138
That was cool.

238
01:13:29.138 --> 01:13:31.138
And the design was beautiful.

239
01:13:31.138 --> 01:13:34.138
Wow, there is a wow factor in what the church can do.

240
01:13:34.138 --> 01:13:39.138
